window.__finlexDocLoaded(10141,{"id":10141,"articles":[{"id":1000566,"no":"Overview","heading":"Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","text":"Sets out overarching requirements for an entity to disclose material information about sustainability-related risks and opportunities useful to primary users of general purpose financial reports, structured around governance, strategy, risk management, and metrics & targets.","seq":0},{"id":1000567,"no":"IFRS S1.25–53","heading":"Four-Pillar Core Content & Materiality","text":"Built on the TCFD structure, IFRS S1 requires disclosures across FOUR core pillars for all material sustainability-related risks and opportunities:\n• Governance (IFRS S1.26–27): governance bodies/individuals overseeing sustainability risks, skills, reporting cadence, and remuneration linkage.\n• Strategy (IFRS S1.28–42): short/medium/long-term risks & opportunities, business model and value chain effects, current and anticipated financial effects, and resilience.\n• Risk Management (IFRS S1.43–44): processes to identify, assess, prioritise, and monitor sustainability risks and integration with overall enterprise risk management.\n• Metrics & Targets (IFRS S1.45–53): cross-industry and industry-specific metrics (referencing SASB Standards under S1.55) and progress against targets.","seq":1},{"id":1000568,"no":"IFRS S1.17–24 & E1–E6","heading":"Financial Materiality, Connected Information & Transition Reliefs","text":"• Investor-focused materiality (IFRS S1.17–19): aligned with IAS 1/IFRS 18 — information is material if omitting, misstating, or obscuring it could reasonably be expected to influence primary users' decisions.\n• Connected information & reporting boundary (IFRS S1.20–24): same reporting entity and reporting period as the related financial statements.\n• Transition reliefs (IFRS S1.E3–E6): 'climate-first' relief permits reporting only climate-related disclosures (IFRS S2) in the first annual reporting period, plus comparative-period relief.\n• China comparison: China's 《企业可持续披露准则——基本准则（试行）》 adopts the same four-pillar structure while incorporating 'double materiality' (impact materiality + financial materiality).","seq":2},{"id":1000569,"no":"Official Access","heading":"Official Handbook & Reference Entry","text":"Official source (IFRS Foundation (ISSB)): https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s1-general-requirements/\nStatus: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally.","seq":3}]});
